// interpret x: data or a block run fully as code (decision blocks-run-by-call: x() runs a block one level, interpret x
// all of it, x! only unwraps; wiki/full-evaluation.md). The code runs as a program of its own, as eval does (lib/prelude.warp);
// it sees the names where data or a block is written, as a closure does: the interpret_scope extension passes those it
// reads, interpret(x, with: {a: a}) (user 11-13); eval of a text sees only what its `with:` names
global interpret(x: any) := eval_code(text(x))
global interpret(x: any, with names: map) := eval(text(x), with: names)
